              "content": "<p class=\"font-bold text-[16px] text-slate-800 mt-5 mb-2\">1. fable / astonished</p>The [fable] was about a young boy with magic powers. At first nobody believed him, but everyone was [astonished] when he made a cat disappear.</p>instincts / banged\nAfter hearing the bad news, she [banged] her fist on the table in anger. Things would go wrong, her [instincts] told her.</p><p class=\"font-bold text-[16px] text-slate-800 mt-5 mb-2\">2. accustomed / feast</p>Though the food was good, he felt sick after the [feast]. He just wasn't [accustomed] to eating so much at one time.</p>joint / physician\nThe [physician] stretched out my arm, looking at my elbow. He wanted to make sure that my pain wasn't a problem with the [joint].</p><p class=\"font-bold text-[16px] text-slate-800 mt-5 mb-2\">3. affirm / emphasis</p>The university placed a special [emphasis] on student safety. They wanted to [affirm] that they were interested in protecting students.</p>stiff / hollow\nHe wanted to find out where his sister went after school, so he hid in a [hollow] tree in the schoolyard. However, when he came out, he felt [stiff] all over.</p><p class=\"font-bold text-[16px] text-slate-800 mt-5 mb-2\">4. clan / tunes</p>The entire [clan] was excited about her wedding. While they drove to the church, they sang happy [tunes].</p>dim / stroked\nIn the [dim] light, it was hard to find the earring she'd dropped on the floor. She [stroked] the ground until she finally felt it.</p><p class=\"font-bold text-[16px] text-slate-800 mt-5 mb-2\">5. tragic / sacrifices</p>The boy suffered from a [tragic] illness. Still, his family made [sacrifices] to make sure he was always comfortable.</p>leak / glowing\nHe shut the door to make sure that no light could [leak] into the room. However, he could still see the moon [glowing] outside of his window.</p>",
